 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, `ATTEMPTS` in `larder/capture.py`. Before each new
+attempt larder waits 2 seconds times the number of attempts made so far, `BACKOFF_SECONDS`: 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds,
+up to 20 seconds in all, which the member spends waiting on the confirmation page. When the last attempt times out,
+the capture fails with `GatewayTimeout`.
+
+Until issue 40 a capture made 3 attempts back to back. The gateway answers slowly every Friday from 17:00 to 19:00,
+its peak, and the 3 attempts went out within a second, so all of them landed in the same slow minute: one Friday 58
+pantry orders were confirmed but never charged, and a payments volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway's
+dashboard the next morning. Switching gateways was ruled out while the contract runs, to December 2026. Replaying
+that Friday's timeouts against the gateway's sandbox with 5 attempts spaced 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds apart, 57 of the
+58 went through; the 20 seconds a member may wait were judged better than capturing the orders by hand.
 
